Stop Vertex Imagen streams from panicking on a nil scanner.

The Imagen stream path reads the whole response and never creates a
scanner, but the pending-filter flush calls scanner.Err() without
checking for that. Every Imagen stream through the service-account or
API-key path dereferences nil and kills the process. This adds the same
isImagenModel(baseModel) guard the neighbouring checks already use.

Works around upstream e049c336b6c2 (fix(vertex): normalize Imagen
predict protocol), present in CPA 8.1.2. Drop it once an upstream
release guards these two calls.

--- a/internal/runtime/executor/gemini_vertex_executor.go
+++ b/internal/runtime/executor/gemini_vertex_executor.go
@@ -1144,7 +1144,7 @@
 			}
 			return
 		}
-		if scanner.Err() == nil && len(pendingFilterLine) > 0 {
+		if (isImagenModel(baseModel) || scanner.Err() == nil) && len(pendingFilterLine) > 0 {
 			if !guardAndEmitLine(pendingFilterLine) {
 				return
 			}
@@ -1560,7 +1560,7 @@
 			}
 			return
 		}
-		if scanner.Err() == nil && len(pendingFilterLine) > 0 {
+		if (isImagenModel(baseModel) || scanner.Err() == nil) && len(pendingFilterLine) > 0 {
 			if !guardAndEmitLine(pendingFilterLine) {
 				return
 			}
